1
00:00:00,115 --> 00:00:01,920
A Short Guide to Home Composting.

2
00:00:02,499 --> 00:00:06,599
Composting turns kitchen and garden waste into rich soil.

3
00:00:06,674 --> 00:00:11,324
It needs very little equipment, and most of the work is done by tiny organisms that

4
00:00:11,374 --> 00:00:12,499
are already around you.

5
00:00:13,188 --> 00:00:14,307
What goes in the bin.

6
00:00:14,881 --> 00:00:18,381
A healthy compost heap needs two kinds of material.

7
00:00:18,481 --> 00:00:21,656
Green materials are wet and rich in nitrogen.

8
00:00:21,731 --> 00:00:24,806
Brown materials are dry and rich in carbon.

9
00:00:24,881 --> 00:00:27,800
Aim for roughly one part green to two parts brown.

10
00:00:28,453 --> 00:00:32,209
Green: vegetable peelings, coffee grounds, fresh grass clippings.

11
00:00:32,871 --> 00:00:36,089
Brown: dry leaves, cardboard, straw, torn paper.

12
00:00:36,698 --> 00:00:40,469
Keep out: meat, dairy, oils, and anything treated with chemicals.

13
00:00:41,171 --> 00:00:42,265
Keeping it healthy.

14
00:00:42,819 --> 00:00:46,369
Turn the heap every week or two so that air reaches the middle.

15
00:00:46,419 --> 00:00:49,144
The pile should feel like a wrung-out sponge.

16
00:00:49,219 --> 00:00:52,044
If it is too wet, add more brown material.

17
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:54,458
If it is too dry, sprinkle it with water.

18
00:00:55,087 --> 00:00:57,412
Patience is the secret ingredient.

19
00:00:57,487 --> 00:00:59,925
Most piles need between two and six months.

20
00:01:00,589 --> 00:01:05,014
A simple way to track the temperature is a small script that logs a reading each

21
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:05,337
day:

22
00:01:05,866 --> 00:01:07,006
Code block skipped.

23
00:01:07,635 --> 00:01:11,206
More tips are collected at link for anyone who wants to read further.

24
00:01:11,865 --> 00:01:13,389
Using the finished compost.

25
00:01:14,024 --> 00:01:18,399
Finished compost is dark, crumbly, and smells like a forest floor.

26
00:01:18,499 --> 00:01:23,074
Spread a thin layer over flower beds, or mix a handful into the soil when planting

27
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:24,299
vegetables.

28
00:01:24,374 --> 00:01:25,642
Your garden will thank you.
